   "html": "<p class=\"ds-dis\"><button disabled>Save name</button><span>Sign in at the top of the page to save.</span></p>",
   "css": ".ds-dis{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;margin:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;align-items:center;color:var(--warn,#7d4b00)}.ds-dis button{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600;border:0;border-radius:6px;min-height:44px;padding:9px 18px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s;background:transparent;color:var(--soft,#2d5468);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--foot,#5b7f91);cursor:default}"
  },
  {
   "name": "Field",
   "kind": "input",
   "refersTo": "field",
   "description": "Label above, value below, 2px foot.",
   "html": "<label class=\"ds-f\">Baud rate<input value=\"9600\"></label>",
   "css": ".ds-f{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;display:block;font-size:.9375rem;color:var(--soft,#2d5468)}.ds-f input{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink,#0b2230);display:block;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;margin-top:4px;padding:9px 12px;border:0;border-bottom:2px solid var(--foot,#5b7f91);border-radius:6px 6px 2px 2px;background:var(--well,#eaf3f7);caret-color:var(--sea,#1683b8);min-height:44px;transition:border-color .15s}.ds-f input:hover,.ds-f input:focus{border-color:var(--sea,#1683b8)}.ds-f input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sea,#1683b8);outline-offset:2px}"
  },
  {
   "name": "Checkbox with consequence",
   "kind": "input",
   "refersTo": "field",
   "description": "A setting and what it does.",
   "html": "<label class=\"ds-c\"><input type=\"checkbox\" checked><span>Listen only<span>Nothing is sent on the line.</span></span></label>",
   "css": ".ds-c{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--ink,#0b2230);max-width:62ch}.ds-c input{width:20px;height:20px;margin:2px 0 0;flex:none;accent-color:var(--accent,#0d4a68)}.ds-c input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sea,#1683b8);outline-offset:2px}.ds-c span span{display:block;color:var(--soft,#2d5468);font-size:.875rem}"
  },
  {
   "name": "Station groups",
   "kind": "nav",
   "refersTo": "station-group",
   "description": "The list is the navigation: ports, then config.",
   "html": "<div class=\"ds-g\"><h2>Ports</h2><a href=\"#\" aria-current=\"true\"><b>1 TigoBus</b><em>Idle</em></a><a href=\"#\"><b>2 Port 2</b><em>Off</em></a><h2>Config</h2><a href=\"#\"><b>MQTT</b><em>Connected</em></a></div>",
   "css": ".ds-g{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;max-width:360px}.ds-g h2{font-size:.875rem;font-weight:650;color:var(--soft,#2d5468);margin:22px 16px 6px}.ds-g h2:first-child{margin-top:0}.ds-g a{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;min-height:50px;align-items:center;padding:8px 16px;margin-bottom:4px;border-radius:8px;color:var(--ink,#0b2230);text-decoration:none;transition:background .15s}.ds-g a[aria-current]{background:var(--sheet,#ffffff)}.ds-g b{font-weight:650;font-size:1.0625rem}.ds-g em{font-style:normal;color:var(--soft,#2d5468)}.ds-g a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sea,#1683b8);outline-offset:2px}"
  },
  {
   "name": "Traffic chart",
   "kind": "custom",
   "refersTo": "chart",
   "description": "Ten minutes, one series, in a well.",
   "html": "<div class=\"ds-ch\"><div><b>Heard, last 10 minutes</b><span>Peak 2.1 kB/s</span></div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sample traffic\"><path class=\"g\" d=\"M0 10H400M0 60H400M0 110H400\"/><path class=\"a\" d=\"M0 110L0 60L60 57L120 62L180 58L200 60L206 110L216 110L222 60L280 57L340 61L400 58L400 110Z\"/><path class=\"l\" d=\"M0 60L60 57L120 62L180 58L200 60L206 110L216 110L222 60L280 57L340 61L400 58\"/><path class=\"e\" d=\"M300 99l6 11h-12z\"/></svg></div>",
   "css": ".ds-ch{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;background:var(--well,#eaf3f7);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px 10px;color:var(--soft,#2d5468)}.ds-ch div{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:2px 16px;justify-content:space-between}.ds-ch b{color:var(--ink,#0b2230);font-weight:650}.ds-ch svg{display:block;width:100%}.ds-ch .g{stroke:var(--rule,#c3d7e1);fill:none}.ds-ch .a{fill:var(--sea,#1683b8);opacity:.14}.ds-ch .l{fill:none;stroke:var(--sea,#1683b8);stroke-width:2;stroke-linejoin:round}.ds-ch .e{fill:var(--warn,#7d4b00)}"
  },
  {
   "name": "Notice",
   "kind": "custom",
   "refersTo": "notice-warn",
   "description": "Something will happen unless you act.",
   "html": "<div class=\"ds-w\"><p>New network settings are on trial.</p><button>Keep settings</button></div>",
   "css": ".ds-w{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 18px;align-items:center;background:var(--warn-bg,#fdf0d6);color:var(--warn,#7d4b00)}.ds-w p{margin:0;flex:1 1 320px}.ds-w button{font:16px/1.45 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600;border:0;border-radius:6px;min-height:44px;padding:9px 18px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s;background:var(--sheet,#ffffff);color:var(--ink,#0b2230)}.ds-w button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sea,#1683b8);outline-offset:2px}"
  }
 ],
 "narrative": {
  "northStar": "Station Reports",
  "overview": "Marine area forecasts: a fixed list of stations, each with its condition, and a report you read in one sentence. Every part of the gateway is a station that reports its own condition. The list says whether the gateway is healthy before anything is clicked; the sheet says what one part is doing and what went wrong.\n\nThe page is plain and exact, calm, and friendly but brief. Three flat sea-blue surfaces carry it: a deep shell, a pale ground, and one sheet. Saturated colour on top of them means a state, something that can be operated, or measured traffic.\n\nIt must never look like the vendor's old web UI (frames and grey forms), and it must never look like a marketing dashboard (big number tiles, gradients, charts for show).",
  "keyCharacteristics": [
   "A verdict, then a list in a fixed order, then one report.",
   "State marked by shape, word and colour together.",
   "One heavy system sans with tabular figures; live values never move the layout.",
   "Flat. One sheet on one ground, told apart by tone.",
   "Light and dark follow the viewer's setting, with the same roles in both.",
   "Controls are sturdy and deliberate: 44px, clear shapes.",
   "Terse, facts only. No internet assets."
  ],
  "rules": [
   {
    "name": "The State-Only Rule",
    "body": "Green, amber and red appear only for state, never as decoration or category. Colour belongs to state and to what can be operated.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Mark-and-Word Rule",
    "body": "State is never colour alone. Every station has a mark, and a word or reading beside it: disc running, ring idle, triangle caution, square fault. Elsewhere a state is stated in words, and colour repeats it.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Logo Wire Rule",
    "body": "The orange wire in the logo is the live part. The terminal's green is not the page's running green, and neither palette borrows from the other.",
    "section": "colors"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Steady Figures Rule",
    "body": "Figures are tabular everywhere.",
    "section": "typography"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Plain Sentence Rule",
    "body": "A report is short declarative sentences, facts only: who it is connected to, what it hears, what went wrong. The register is plain and a little formal: no idioms (\"all good\", \"by itself\"), \"responding\" not \"answering\", \"reverts\" not \"goes back\". The product's own terms stay: heard, sent, turned away, station.",
    "section": "typography"
   },
   {
    "name": "The Still List Rule",
    "body": "Live values change in place. Stations never reorder or move by severity: a fault fills its own row and is named in the verdict.",
    "section": "layout"
   },
   {
    "name": "The One Sheet Rule",
    "body": "There is one sheet. Nothing inside it is another card; sections are separated by space and a heading.",
    "section": "elevation & depth"
   }
  ],
  "dos": [
   "**Do** pair every state colour with a word, and in the list with its mark too.",
   "**Do** name a fault in words, in the verdict and on its station.",
   "**Do** reserve space for live text, and use tabular figures.",
   "**Do** keep one primary button per form, and say beside a disabled save what unlocks it.",
   "**Do** use the same roles in light and dark; change values, not meaning.",
   "**Do** put everything in the page itself: inline drawing, no internet assets.",
   "**Do** stay terse: facts, and the consequences that matter."
  ],
  "donts": [
   "**Don't** look like the vendor's old web UI: frames, grey forms.",
   "**Don't** look like a marketing dashboard: big number tiles, gradients, charts for show.",
   "**Don't** use green, amber or red for anything but state.",
   "**Don't** use the disc, ring, triangle or square as decoration.",
   "**Don't** reorder the list by severity.",
   "**Don't** add shadows, or a card inside the sheet.",
   "**Don't** bring the logo's green or orange into the page.",
   "**Don't** animate anything but colour."
  ]
 }
}
